  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "get_coffset",
    "file": "c-blosc2/blosc/frame.c",
    "description": "`get_coffset` validates a decoded nonnegative chunk offset only with `offset > frame->len`, even though contiguous-frame callers interpret it relative to the end of the frame header (`frame->cframe + header_len + offset`). It therefore accepts offsets whose relative value is no larger than the total frame length but whose actual pointer, `header_len + offset`, lies outside the supplied frame. In this PoV, `frame_get_lazychunk` uses that accepted offset and `sw32_` reads the chunk `cbytes` field from the out-of-bounds pointer at frame.c:1972-1973. Validation must account for `header_len`, overflow, and enough remaining bytes for the chunk header/field before returning the offset.",
    "conditions": "An attacker-controlled in-memory frame must pass the basic frame parsing checks (including encoded frame length matching the input, valid frame type/trailer, and header-derived positive chunk count) and contain an offsets chunk that decodes the requested chunk's offset to a nonnegative value `<= frame->len`, while `header_len + offset + BLOSC2_CHUNK_CBYTES + sizeof(int32_t) > frame->len` (or the addition overflows). The fuzzer imports the input without copying via `blosc2_schunk_from_buffer`, then requests chunk 0; the malicious decoded offset passes `get_coffset` and is dereferenced by `frame_get_lazychunk`, causing the 4-byte heap-buffer-overflow."
  },
